---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Home">
  <section class="flex flex-col gap-8">
    <div class="flex gap-8 items-start">
      <img
        src="/profile.jpg"
        alt="Tara Mishra"
        class="w-32 h-32 rounded-full object-cover flex-shrink-0"
      />
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
        <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold">Dr Tara Mishra</h1>
        <p class="text-gray-500">Project Scientist · National Center for Electron Microscopy, Molecular Foundry · Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory</p>
        <div class="flex gap-3 text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 flex-wrap">
          <a href="mailto:tpmishra@lbl.gov" class="underline hover:text-black">Email</a>
          <span>·</span>
          <a href="/cv.pdf" class="underline hover:text-black">CV</a>
          <span>·</span>
          <a href="https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3000-2555" class="underline hover:text-black" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ORCID</a>
          <span>·</span>
          <a href="https://github.com/taramatsci" class="underline hover:text-black" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
          <span>·</span>
          <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=vtbEcEsAAAAJ&hl=en" class="underline hover:text-black" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Scholar</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        I am a Project Scientist at the
        <a href="https://foundry.lbl.gov/about/facilities/the-national-center-for-electron-microscopy-ncem/" class="underline hover:text-black" target="_blank" rel="noopener">National Center for Electron Microscopy (NCEM)</a>
        at the
        <a href="https://foundry.lbl.gov" class="underline hover:text-black" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Molecular Foundry</a>,
        Lawrence Berkeley National Laboratory.
        My research specializes in advanced electron microscopy for energy materials and the
        automation of electron microscopy characterization. My expertise encompasses
        aberration-corrected STEM imaging, EELS spectroscopy, 4D-STEM, and X-ray characterization,
        with a particular focus on battery and semiconductor materials.
      </p>
      <p>
        I am actively engaged in developing autonomous characterization techniques and software
        toolkits for image analysis and data processing of complex microscopy signals. A central
        goal of my work is to bridge atomic-scale structure with macroscopic materials performance —
        understanding how local chemistry, defects, and microstructural heterogeneity govern the
        behavior of next-generation energy materials such as disordered rocksalt cathodes and
        solid electrolytes.
      </p>
      <p>
        I completed my postdoctoral training with the
        <a href="https://ceder.berkeley.edu" class="underline hover:text-black" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ceder Group</a>
        at UC Berkeley and LBNL, where I applied multimodal electron microscopy to study
        Li-ion cathodes and solid-state electrolytes.
        I received my Ph.D. from the
        <a href="https://www.nus.edu.sg" class="underline hover:text-black" target="_blank" rel="noopener">National University of Singapore</a>
        (2018–2022), where I bridged atomic-scale computational modeling — including DFT,
        thermodynamic analysis, and kinetic Monte Carlo simulations — with high-resolution
        electron microscopy to study III-Nitride LED materials.
      </p>
      <p>
        Driven by the goal of innovating future materials through atomic engineering, I take an
        interdisciplinary approach that integrates microscopy, computational modeling, and advanced
        characterization. I am passionate about developing large-scale data workflows and open-source
        toolkits that accelerate materials discovery.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
